From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@wisc.edu>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Store the group name in GroupNotFound

The GroupNotFound(fname, gname) constructor dropped gname, so what()
reported "the group  not found in the file ..." with an empty group
name.

---
 src/pyne.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/pyne.h b/src/pyne.h
index cf3f4ea..6eda061 100644
--- a/src/pyne.h
+++ b/src/pyne.h
@@ -415,6 +415,7 @@ namespace h5wrap
     GroupNotFound(std::string fname, std::string gname)
     {
       filename = fname;
+      groupname = gname;
     };
 
     /// helpful error message that includes the filename and the groupname
